This project has no runtime dependencies. The analysis uses Python's own `ast`
module, which is deliberate: the tool is meant to run in someone else's CI, on a
codebase its author has never seen, and every dependency is a reason it will not
install there.

Development-only dependencies, installed from PyPI by the user, keep their own
licences:

  ruff   MIT

Why Apache-2.0 rather than the proprietary source-available terms used across
the rest of this author's work: this is a tool intended to be run by other
people in their own pipelines. Terms forbidding use would make it unusable for
its stated purpose. The express patent grant in section 3 is also load-bearing
here, given existing patents in the adjacent area of parallel mutation testing.
